  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is implicated in the regulation of Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Calcium;4-Oxopentanoate;Dihydrate, Npc115753, and 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid. These compounds all share a common target of DO4, suggesting a potential mechanistic link between Corticatic Acid E and DO4 through the modulation of this kinase. The evidence is supported by a consistent pathway where Corticatic Acid E acts as a target of multiple compounds that are themselves targets of DO4, indicating a possible role in the regulation of the kinase. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Corticatic Acid E and DO4. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition or regulation of a shared target, which could be a key pathway in the biological process underlying the observed effects.",
